ll 2021-Spring 2022\nSeminars\nSeminar Schedule\nSeminar Recordings\nHome \u00bb Introduction to Graduate Programs \u00bb Doctor of Philosophy\nDoctor of Philosophy\nThe degree of Doctor of Philosophy is awarded in recognition of in-depth knowledge in a major field and comprehensive understanding of related subjects together with a demonstration of ability to perform independent investigation and to communicate the results of such investigation in an acceptable dissertation.\nStudents entering with a Bachelor\u2019s degree will satisfactorily complete a minimum of 36 credit hours (which may include the independent study/research, course BIOL 601), tutorials, and seminars. For students entering with an approved Master\u2019s degree, completion of at least 18 semester hours of course work is required. After completing required coursework, a minimum of 18 semester hours of dissertation research (BIOL 701) is required for all doctoral students.\nDoctoral Program Guidelines and Rules\nDepartment of Biology\nCase Western Reserve University\nDeGrace Hall\n2080 Adelbert Road\nCleveland, OH 44106\n216.368.3557\nSite Feedback\nLegal Notice | Privacy Policy\nTitle IX Notice of Non-Discrimination\nSocial Media\nFacebook\nCWRU LINKS\nApply\nGive\nVisit\nDirectory\nScroll To Top", "links": [["About", "https://biology.case.edu/"], ["Faculty and Staff", "https://biology.case.edu/faculty-and-staff/"], ["Graduate Students", "https://biology.case.edu/graduate-students/"], ["Contact", "https://biology.case.edu/about-us/contact/"], ["Forms and Resources for Faculty", "https://biology.case.edu/faculty-and-staff/forms-and-resources-for-faculty/"], ["Undergraduate", "https://biology.case.edu/undergraduate/"], ["Independent Research in Biology", "https://biology.case.edu/undergraduate/independent-research-in-biology/"], ["Honors in Biology", "https://biology.case.edu/undergraduate/honors-in-biology/"], ["Honors in Neuroscience", "https://biology.case.edu/honors-in-neuroscience/"], ["Michels